{%- comment -%}
ART AVENUE — PRODUCT IMAGE ALT-TEXT CONVENTION
Apply to every product image at creation time. Alt text is set on the MediaImage
via the `fileUpdate` mutation (input: { id, alt }). IDs come from
product.media -> ... on MediaImage { id }.

WHY: empty alt = SEO + accessibility miss. Consistent alt = repeatable, scalable,
and safe (no per-image guessing about what the photo shows).

PATTERN
-------
  {Product name} — {material/construction} {piece type} by Art Avenue{, shot suffix}

  - Base (everything before the suffix) is IDENTICAL on every image of the product.
    It carries the SEO weight: product name + key material terms + brand.
  - First/primary image: NO suffix (cleanest for the main listing image).
  - Every other image: add a short, SHOT-NEUTRAL suffix for accessibility distinctness.

SHOT SUFFIXES (use only what is verifiable without seeing the photo)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
  Generic, always safe:   view 2, view 3, view 4, ...
  Safe descriptors:       hardware detail, corner detail, texture detail,
                          closure detail, in a styled setting, made to order
  AVOID claiming specifics you cannot verify from the filename alone
  (e.g. "open interior", "brass corners", "leather vs kilim") unless you have
  confirmed which image is which. Shot-neutral beats wrong.

RULES
-----
  - Keep under ~125 characters.
  - Do NOT keyword-stuff: the base already repeats the key terms across images;
    that is sufficient. Do not pile synonyms into the suffix.
  - One language (storefront English).
  - Never start with "image of" / "photo of" (screen readers already announce it).

EXAMPLE — Jaisalmer Campaign Trunk (storage pilot)
--------------------------------------------------
  img 1: Jaisalmer Campaign Trunk — handcrafted leather and kilim trunk by Art Avenue
  img 2: Jaisalmer Campaign Trunk — handcrafted leather and kilim trunk by Art Avenue, view 2
  img n: Jaisalmer Campaign Trunk — handcrafted leather and kilim trunk by Art Avenue, hardware detail

MUTATION SHAPE
--------------
  mutation Alt($files: [FileUpdateInput!]!) {
    fileUpdate(files: $files) {
      files { ... on MediaImage { id alt } }
      userErrors { field message code }
    }
  }
  variables.files = [ { id: "gid://shopify/MediaImage/...", alt: "..." }, ... ]
  (fileUpdate accepts the full batch in one call.)
{%- endcomment -%}
